# Retail Return Intelligence — Frontend Design System & Architecture Rules

You are working on the Retail Return Intelligence system. Follow these rules strictly when generating, modifying, or refactoring frontend code.

## 1. Mandatory Shadcn/UI Nova Component Usage (`@/components/ui/*`)
- **NEVER use raw HTML interactive elements**:
  - `<button>` is STRICTLY FORBIDDEN -> Use `<Button>` from `@/components/ui/button`.
  - `<input>` is STRICTLY FORBIDDEN -> Use `<Input>` from `@/components/ui/input`.
  - `<kbd>` is STRICTLY FORBIDDEN -> Use `<Kbd>` from `@/components/ui/kbd`.
  - `<textarea>` is STRICTLY FORBIDDEN -> Use `<Textarea>` from `@/components/ui/textarea`.
  - `<select>` is STRICTLY FORBIDDEN -> Use `<Select>` from `@/components/ui/select`.
- **Avatars**:
  - NEVER render user, customer, or agent initials or profiles with plain text/divs.
  - ALWAYS use `<Avatar>`, `<AvatarFallback>`, and `<AvatarBadge>` from `@/components/ui/avatar`.
- **Empty States**:
  - When search results or lists have 0 items, use `<Empty>`, `<EmptyMedia>`, `<EmptyHeader>`, `<EmptyTitle>`, `<EmptyDescription>` from `@/components/ui/empty`.
- **Loading Indicators**:
  - Use `<Spinner>` from `@/components/ui/spinner`.
- **Badges & Tags**:
  - Use `<Badge>` from `@/components/ui/badge` with `variant="outline"` or `variant="secondary"`.
- **Cards & Containers**:
  - Use `<Card>`, `<CardHeader>`, `<CardTitle>`, `<CardDescription>`, `<CardContent>` from `@/components/ui/card`.
- **Tabs**:
  - Use `<Tabs>`, `<TabsList>`, `<TabsTrigger>`, `<TabsContent>` from `@/components/ui/tabs`.

## 2. Visual Aesthetics & Tokens (`design.md`)
- **Canvas**: Pure Paper White (`#ffffff`, `bg-white`).
- **Hairline Borders**: `border border-neutral-200` (`#e5e5e5`).
- **Secondary Surfaces**: `bg-neutral-50` or `bg-neutral-100`.
- **Pill Geometry**: Outer search pills, top navigation tabs, status chips, and filter toggles must adhere to `rounded-full` or `rounded-xl` / `rounded-2xl` card containers.
- **Typography**:
  - Headings & Body: Inter / Sans (`font-sans`).
  - IDs, Metrics, Timestamps, Keys, Labels: JetBrains Mono (`font-mono`, `uppercase`, `tracking-wider`).

## 3. Enforcement
These rules are enforced by ESLint rule `react/forbid-elements` in `frontend/eslint.config.js` and Husky pre-commit hooks. Any code with raw elements will fail linting and commit verification. Always run `npm run lint` and `npm run build` in `frontend/` before completing your work.
